== Notes ==

*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]].
*The forms are drow warrior, kobold commando, and lizardman. These are replaced by stronger epic versions at shifter level 17.
*At shifter level 13, unlimited uses of this ability are gained via [[infinite greater wildshape|infinite humanoid shape]].
*This form of shapeshifting cannot be [[dispel]]led.
*Only the highest AC bonus from items will merge.
*[[Off-hand]] weapon properties never merge, nor do properties from bracers/gauntlets/gloves.
*The kobold commando has a bonus to setting traps, but trap kits (like most other items) cannot be used while shifted. Similarly, the form has a use poison bonus feat, but a shifted PC will be unable to use a [[Poison (item)|poison item]] to apply poison to a weapon.
*The kobold commando shape provides the [[sneak attack]] ability. This will not [[stack]] with a character's sneak attack from [[rogue]] levels, but it will stack with a [[sneak attack, blackguard|blackguard's sneak attack]] or an [[assassin]]'s [[death attack]].
*The drow warrior shape changes a shifter's race to [[elf]] for the duration of the shift, which can cause a [[multiclass penalty]] for a shifter with a second [[base class]] (in addition to the necessary [[druid]]), even if no such penalty exists for the shifter's original race.
*The constitution score while in (epic) drow warrior form reflects the -2 penalty of the elven race and discounts the bonus/penalty of a shifter's normal race. However, this change is cosmetic only (appearing only on the character sheet) and does not affect the stats based upon constitution (hit points, fortitude save, and concentration) unless the constitution score is in any way subsequently changed. Such subsequent changes to the constitution score include those resulting from item merge, later potion buffs, and spell expiration.

